## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## SWIFT & iOS DEVELOPMENT STANDARDS
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Language Requirements
- **Swift 5.9+** ONLY - Use latest features
- **SwiftUI** for all UI - No UIKit unless absolutely necessary
- **async/await** for ALL async operations - No callbacks
- **Protocol-oriented** - Protocols over inheritance
- **Value types** (struct) over reference types (class) by default
- Use `final` on classes that won't be subclassed
- **Prefer `let` over `var`** - Immutability prevents bugs

### Naming Conventions (Apple Style Guide)
```swift
// Variables & Functions: camelCase
func generateDeck(from: WizardState) async throws -> Deck
let isGenerating: Bool
var deckCount: Int

// Types: PascalCase
struct DeckGenerationService { }
class WizardViewModel: ObservableObject { }
enum SubscriptionTier { }

// Booleans: is/has/should/can prefix
let isLoading: Bool
let hasCompletedOnboarding: Bool
let shouldShowPaywall: Bool
let canAccessFeature: Bool

// Methods: Start with verbs
func uploadDocument() async throws
func validateInput() -> Bool
func incrementDeckCount()

// Constants: Descriptive camelCase
let maxSlideCount = 30
let defaultTimeout: TimeInterval = 10.0

// Enums: Lowercase cases
enum DeckUseCase {
    case investor  // ✅ Good
    case Investor  // ❌ Bad
}
```

### Architecture: MVVM + Services

```
Views/ (SwiftUI)
├── DeckListView.swift          # UI ONLY, no business logic
├── DeckDetailView.swift
├── WizardContainerView.swift
└── Components/
    ├── InputField.swift
    └── PrimaryButton.swift

ViewModels/ (@MainActor + ObservableObject)
├── DeckListViewModel.swift     # Business logic, @Published properties
├── DeckDetailViewModel.swift
└── WizardViewModel.swift

Models/ (Codable structs)
├── Deck.swift                  # Pure data, no logic
├── Slide.swift
├── Theme.swift
├── SubscriptionTier.swift
└── AcceleratorTemplate.swift

Services/ (Protocol-based)
├── Firebase/
│   ├── AuthService.swift       # Firebase Auth wrapper
│   ├── FirestoreService.swift  # Database operations
│   └── StorageService.swift    # File uploads
├── AI/
│   ├── DeckGenerationService.swift      # GPT-4/5 deck generation
│   └── EliteDocumentAnalyzer.swift      # Document analysis
├── SubscriptionService.swift   # RevenueCat/StoreKit
└── DocumentUploadService.swift # Document processing
```

### SwiftUI Best Practices

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT: Clean, readable, performant
struct DeckListView: View {
    @StateObject private var viewModel = DeckListViewModel()
    @State private var showingWizard = false
    
    var body: some View {
        NavigationStack {
            deckList
                .navigationTitle("My Decks")
                .toolbar { toolbar }
        }
        .sheet(isPresented: $showingWizard) {
            WizardContainerView()
        }
    }
    
    private var deckList: some View {
        List(viewModel.decks) { deck in
            DeckCard(deck: deck)
        }
    }
    
    @ToolbarContentBuilder
    private var toolbar: some ToolbarContent {
        ToolbarItem(placement: .primaryAction) {
            Button { showingWizard = true } label: {
                Image(systemName: "plus.circle.fill")
            }
        }
    }
}

// ❌ WRONG: Massive body, hard to read
struct DeckListView: View {
    var body: some View {
        // 500 lines of code here...
    }
}
```

**State Management:**
- `@State` - View-local state (private)
- `@StateObject` - View creates the ObservableObject
- `@ObservedObject` - Parent passes the ObservableObject
- `@EnvironmentObject` - App-wide shared state (use sparingly)
- `@Published` - In ViewModels for reactive updates

### Concurrency (async/await)

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT: Clean async/await
@MainActor
func generateDeck() async throws {
    isLoading = true
    defer { isLoading = false }
    
    let deck = try await deckService.generate(from: wizardState)
    generatedDeck = deck
}

// ❌ WRONG: Completion handlers (old style)
func generateDeck(completion: @escaping (Result<Deck, Error>) -> Void) {
    // Don't do this anymore
}
```

**Concurrency Rules:**
- Mark ViewModels with `@MainActor` - UI updates on main thread
- Use `Task { }` for fire-and-forget work
- Use `async let` for concurrent operations
- Use `TaskGroup` for multiple concurrent ops with results
- ALWAYS handle cancellation
- Use `.task { }` modifier for view-scoped async work

### Error Handling

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT: Custom errors, clear messages
enum DeckGenerationError: Error, LocalizedError {
    case invalidInput(String)
    case aiServiceUnavailable
    case networkTimeout
    
    var errorDescription: String? {
        switch self {
        case .invalidInput(let field):
            return "Please provide valid \(field)"
        case .aiServiceUnavailable:
            return "AI service is temporarily unavailable"
        case .networkTimeout:
            return "Request timed out. Check your connection."
        }
    }
}

// Use throws for errors that should propagate
func uploadDocument(url: URL) async throws -> DocumentUpload

// Use Result for operations that can fail
func validateWizardState() -> Result<Void, ValidationError>

// ❌ WRONG: Generic errors, no context
throw NSError(domain: "Error", code: -1, userInfo: nil)
```

**Error UI Rules:**
- ALWAYS show user-friendly messages (never raw errors)
- Provide actionable solutions ("Try again" button)
- Log errors to Crashlytics with context
- Never fail silently

