## XCODE BUILD OPTIMIZATION (FASTEST BUILDS IN THE WORLD)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Build Settings for MAXIMUM SPEED

**In Xcode Build Settings:**

```
# Compilation Settings
SWIFT_COMPILATION_MODE = Incremental (Debug), Whole Module (Release)
SWIFT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = -Onone (Debug), -O (Release)
SWIFT_WHOLE_MODULE_OPTIMIZATION = YES (Release only)
COMPILER_INDEX_STORE_ENABLE = NO (for faster builds)
DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT = dwarf (Debug), dwarf-with-dsym (Release)

# Parallel Builds
ENABLE_ONLY_ACTIVE_RESOURCES = YES
ENABLE_PARALLEL_TESTING = YES

# Speed Optimizations
GCC_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = 0 (Debug), s (Release)
ENABLE_BITCODE = NO
ENABLE_TESTABILITY = YES (Debug only)

# Module Settings
DEFINES_MODULE = YES
CLANG_ENABLE_MODULES = YES
CLANG_ENABLE_MODULE_DEBUGGING = YES

# Link Time Optimization
LLVM_LTO = NO (Debug), monolithic (Release)
```

### Terminal Commands for LIGHTNING FAST Builds

```bash
# Clean build (when needed)
xcodebuild clean -project "Pitch Me.xcodeproj" -scheme "Pitch Me"

# Fast incremental build
xcodebuild build -project "Pitch Me.xcodeproj" -scheme "Pitch Me" -sdk iphonesimulator -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 15' -parallelizeTargets

# Build with detailed timing
xcodebuild build -project "Pitch Me.xcodeproj" -scheme "Pitch Me" -showBuildTimingSummary

# Archive for release
xcodebuild archive -project "Pitch Me.xcodeproj" -scheme "Pitch Me" -archivePath ./build/PitchMe.xcarchive

# Export IPA
xcodebuild -exportArchive -archivePath ./build/PitchMe.xcarchive -exportPath ./build -exportOptionsPlist ExportOptions.plist
```

### Xcode Shortcuts (SPEED DEMONS ONLY)

```
⌘B          - Build
⌘R          - Run
⌘.          - Stop
⌘K          - Clear console
⌘⇧K         - Clean build folder
⌘⇧O         - Open quickly (navigate to file)
⌘⇧J         - Reveal in project navigator
⌘⌥[         - Move line up
⌘⌥]         - Move line down
⌘/          - Comment/uncomment
⌘⌃E         - Edit all in scope
⌘⌥⇧K        - Clean derived data (nuclear option)
```

### Derived Data Management

```bash
# Location of derived data
~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData

# Clear derived data (when builds are weird)
rm -rf ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData

# Set custom derived data location (for faster builds on SSD)
# Xcode → Settings → Locations → Derived Data → Custom
```

### Simulator Management

```bash
# List all simulators
xcrun simctl list

# Boot simulator
xcrun simctl boot "iPhone 15"

# Reset simulator (fixes many issues)
xcrun simctl erase all

# Delete unavailable simulators
xcrun simctl delete unavailable
```

### Debug Faster

```swift
// MARK: - Debug Helpers

#if DEBUG
// Print with file and line
func debugPrint(_ message: String, file: String = #file, line: Int = #line) {
    print("[\(file.components(separatedBy: "/").last ?? ""):\(line)] \(message)")
}

// Measure execution time
func measure(_ label: String, block: () -> Void) {
    let start = CFAbsoluteTimeGetCurrent()
    block()
    let duration = CFAbsoluteTimeGetCurrent() - start
    print("⏱️ \(label): \(duration)s")
}
#endif
```

### Breakpoint Tricks

```
# Symbolic breakpoint for all exceptions
Exception: All
Action: Log message

# Breakpoint on method
-[UIViewController viewDidLoad]

# Conditional breakpoint
Condition: count > 100
```

### Instruments (Profiling)

```bash
# Profile app launch time
instruments -t "App Launch" -D launch.trace YourApp.app

# Profile memory leaks
instruments -t "Leaks" -D leaks.trace YourApp.app

# Profile time profiler
instruments -t "Time Profiler" -D profile.trace YourApp.app
```

### Build Optimization Checklist

Before Release:
- [ ] Enable whole module optimization
- [ ] Strip debug symbols
- [ ] Enable bitcode (if needed)
- [ ] Optimize PNG files
- [ ] Remove unused code
- [ ] Profile with Instruments
- [ ] Test on real device
- [ ] Check app size

For Faster Debug Builds:
- [ ] Disable optimization (`-Onone`)
- [ ] Use dwarf (not dwarf-with-dsym)
- [ ] Disable module optimization
- [ ] Use incremental compilation
- [ ] Keep derived data

### Common Build Issues & Fixes

```
# "Module not found"
→ Clean build folder (⌘⇧K)
→ Delete derived data
→ Restart Xcode

# "Signing issues"
→ Check bundle ID
→ Update provisioning profile
→ Enable automatic signing

# "Simulator not available"
→ Reset simulator
→ Restart Xcode
→ Check macOS/Xcode version

# "Build takes forever"
→ Check for circular dependencies
→ Reduce Swift compilation complexity
→ Use build time analyzer
→ Break up large files

# "Cannot install on device"
→ Trust development certificate on device
→ Check device iOS version
→ Clean build and retry
```

### Git Integration with Xcode

```bash
# Initialize git (if not done)
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit - Pitch Me v1.0"

# Create .gitignore
echo "DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
.DS_Store
GoogleService-Info.plist
.env" > .gitignore

# Connect to remote
git remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/pitch-me.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

### Swift Build Time Optimization

```swift
// ❌ SLOW: Complex type inference
let numbers = [1, 2, 3].map { $0 * 2 }.filter { $0 > 2 }.map { $0 + 1 }

// ✅ FAST: Break into steps
let doubled = [1, 2, 3].map { $0 * 2 }
let filtered = doubled.filter { $0 > 2 }
let result = filtered.map { $0 + 1 }

// ❌ SLOW: Large SwiftUI body
var body: some View {
    // 500 lines of code
}

// ✅ FAST: Extract to computed properties
var body: some View {
    content
}

private var content: some View {
    // Extracted content
}
```

### Xcode Preferences for Speed

```
Xcode → Settings → Behaviors
- Build Starts: Hide navigator
- Build Succeeds: Show navigator
- Build Fails: Show issues

Xcode → Settings → Text Editing
- Enable syntax coloring
- Enable code folding
- Show line numbers

Xcode → Settings → General
- Reopen last project on launch: OFF (faster)
```

### Build Time Warnings

Add build time warnings for slow files:

```bash
# In Build Settings → Other Swift Flags
-Xfrontend -warn-long-function-bodies=500
-Xfrontend -warn-long-expression-type-checking=500
```

This will warn you if any function takes > 500ms to compile.

### CI/CD Fast Builds (GitHub Actions)

```yaml
name: Build & Test
on: [push, pull_request]
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: macos-latest
    steps:
    - uses: actions/checkout@v2
    - name: Setup Xcode
      uses: maxim-lobanov/setup-xcode@v1
      with:
        xcode-version: latest-stable
    - name: Cache SPM
      uses: actions/cache@v2
      with:
        path: .build
        key: ${{ runner.os }}-spm-${{ hashFiles('**/Package.resolved') }}
    - name: Build
      run: xcodebuild build -scheme "Pitch Me" -sdk iphonesimulator -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 15'
```

